Continue the same source-only design consultation; no formal blueprint promotion and no runtime verdict. New pinned primary-source evidence below materially improves the candidate. Review only the amended source/serialization/baseline claims, not the entire programme. You have no tools here; distinguish newly read sources from the provided command records.

Correct four issues in your preserved earlier answer: the line about restricting backends was wording from my consultation brief, not a quotation from the commissioning document; a new HTTP header alone may be ignored by an older daemon; public LlamaServer.Tokenize passes add_special=false while the actual native chat non-MTMD dispatch passes true,true; and native template inputs can depend on the clock, so matching request JSON across two template renders does not establish identical prepared tokens. A proven flag difference is not an executed model undercount. Preserve the previous report rather than retroactively rewriting it.

The dependency already has /v1/chat/completions/input_tokens using the native chat parser/template and a token-count path. This is source-verified at b10091, NOT runtime-qualified: the version-only executable probe timed out and a follow-up diagnostic was refused before it ran. No model was loaded by this probe and no blocked command was rerouted. The newly selected direction rejects an auxiliary one-token generation as a production tokenizer, uses native non-inferencing preparation/counting, and requires final admission over the actual prepared input before it is queued. The endpoint can inform preview, but does not reserve or prove the future dispatch. OQ-1 remains open for exact versioned ingress, output policy, backend coverage and integration; the document deliberately remains SPEC-DRAFT. It does not silently remove cloud support.

The three golden fixtures are independent literal JSON with Python digests checked against Go standard-library marshal/hash. They are null-binding reference serialization only, not the unimplemented storage/request producer. The recovered HTTP baseline now completes with one existing-settings control pass and one expected feature-boundary failure: instructions PUT gets HTML200, not the requested saved-profile JSON. The CLI really builds, --help succeeds and instructions --help fails unknown-command. No claim of restart/persistence acceptance is made.

Please return (1) any concrete incorrect amended assertion with source counterexample, (2) whether the rejected one-token route has been replaced by a defensible direction rather than new claimed working code, (3) at most four exact remaining design decisions needed before promotion, and (4) corrections to your own earlier wording. Do not invent closure, run count or authority. Under 1200 words. No BLUEPRINT_JUDGE, JUDGE or GATE token.

